## 4. Damage and healing

```paradox
POD_combat_move_set_hp_damage    = { VALUE = @damage_minor }
POD_combat_move_set_morale_damage = { VALUE = @morale_damage_minor }
POD_combat_move_set_self_damage  = { VALUE = @self_damage_tiny }
POD_combat_move_set_hp_heal      = { VALUE = @healing_minor TYPE = superficial }
POD_combat_move_set_morale_heal  = { VALUE = @morale_heal_minor }
```

| Family | Constants |
|---|---|
| HP damage | `@damage_tiny` 1 .. `@damage_maximum` 6 |
| Morale damage | `@morale_damage_tiny` 1 .. `_maximum` 6 |
| Self-damage | `@self_damage_tiny` 1, `_minor` 2, `_medium` 3 |
| HP heal | `@healing_tiny` 1 .. `@healing_massive` 5 |
| Morale heal | `@morale_heal_tiny` 1 .. `_massive` 5 |

`set_hp_heal` takes `TYPE = superficial` or `TYPE = aggravated`. Aggravated
healing also reduces aggravated damage, so it is much more valuable. The heal
type does **not** follow the move's damage class; set it deliberately.

Morale damage has its own auto-hit path: no hit roll, no guard, no soak. It
still respects dodge and stealth.

Self-damage is always superficial and lands on the actor.

---

## 5. Damage class

```paradox
POD_combat_move_set_hp_damage    = { VALUE = @damage_minor }
POD_combat_move_set_damage_class = { VALUE = fire }
```

**Call the class setter after `set_hp_damage`.** `set_hp_damage` stamps
`damage_type = superficial` as part of its own body, so a class written first
is silently overwritten.

| Value | Behaviour |
|---|---|
| `superficial` | The default `set_hp_damage` stamps. Never needs this setter. |
| `aggravated` | Forced aggravated against every target, `REASON = duel_aggravated`. |
| `fire` | Always aggravated against every splat. |
| `lightning` | Always aggravated against every splat. |
| `balefire` | Always aggravated, plus a balefire health modifier stack per point of final damage. |
| `cold`, `sun`, `silver`, `gold`, `holy`, `poison`, `cold_iron` | Aggravated only against their matrix splats; some splats are immune. |

One class per move, single axis. An element rides its own `REASON` into PoD's
health system, which resolves immunity, downgrade and splat multipliers **per
target**.

Anything that classifies aggravated for a given victim is unsoakable without a
bane modifier. So `aggravated`, `fire`, `lightning` and `balefire` bypass soak
universally; the rest bypass it against their matrix splats.

The class is consumed by a direct HP hit, a typed HP counter, a typed HP DoT,
or a `dot` bonus effect. On a move with none of those it is inert.

---

## 6. Delivery capability flags

There is no "attack type" property. Offensive delivery is assembled from four
presence flags.

```paradox
POD_combat_move_set_flag = { NAME = requires_hit_roll }
```

| Flag | Present means |
|---|---|
| `requires_hit_roll` | the attack rolls to hit and can miss |
| `checks_guard` | the target's Guard can block it, and is consumed |
| `checks_stance` | Dodge and Stealth can evade it |
| `checks_spirit_gate` | the physical spirit-contact gate applies (passes harmlessly through incorporeal targets unless the actor can damage spirits) |

**Guard bypass is the absence of `checks_guard`.** There is no bypass-guard
variable; the contact resolver reads the capability flag directly.

Common idioms:

| Idiom | Flags |
|---|---|
| Ordinary physical strike | all four |
| Supernatural blast | `checks_stance` only (auto-hits, ignores guard, reaches spirits) |
| Direct morale attack | `checks_stance` only |
| Contact-based control | `requires_control_contact` + the delivery flags it should respect |
| Guaranteed control | no delivery flags, no `requires_control_contact` |

`requires_control_contact` makes a move with no HP or morale payload missable:
a failed delivery suppresses its debuff tiers, **its buff tiers**, mind
control, and the AP-drain and initiative-debuff mirrors. Stances are applied
regardless. Omit it when the utility effect is meant to be guaranteed.

It is only meaningful on `single_enemy`. Team debuffs and stance strips
broadcast before the one-workspace contact check, so a team move cannot make
every recipient pass contact.

Two destructive overrides, valid even without `checks_stance`:

| Flag | Effect |
|---|---|
| `bypass_dodge` | strip the target's Dodge, then ignore it |
| `bypass_stealth` | break the target's Stealth, then ignore it |

---

## 7. `TARGETING`

| Value | Hits |
|---|---|
| `single_enemy` | one selected enemy; the fully supported mode |
| `single_ally` | one living ally, never the actor |
| `self` | the actor |
| `team_enemy` | every living enemy |
| `team_ally` | every living ally, actor included |
| `team_all` | every living combatant on both sides, actor included |
| `single_pc` | the player character |

### What actually broadcasts

| Payload | single_enemy | single_ally | self | team_enemy | team_ally | team_all |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `hp_damage` | yes | to the enemy | to the enemy | yes | to the enemy | yes, actor included |
| `morale_damage` | yes | to the enemy | to the enemy | yes | to the enemy | yes, actor included |
| `hp_heal` / `morale_heal` | yes | to the ally | to the actor | to the actor | yes | no arm exists |
| soak/hit **buff** tiers | to the actor | to the ally | to the actor | to the actor | yes | no arm exists |
| soak/hit **debuff** tiers | yes | to the ally | to the enemy | yes | no | yes, actor included |
| `set_guard` / `dodge` / `stealth` | to the actor | to the ally | to the actor | to the actor | yes | no arm exists |
| `bypass_dodge` / `bypass_stealth` / `remove_guard` | yes | - | - | yes | no | yes, never self-applied |
| DoT, `mind_control`, `ap_drain`, `initiative_debuff`, `steal_gold` | yes | - | - | **one target only** | **one target only** | **one target only** |
| every non-actor-side bonus effect | yes | - | - | **one target only** | **one target only** | **one target only** |
| retaliation **arming** | yes | yes | yes | yes | yes | yes |
| triggers the victim's armed counter | if it deals HP damage | - | if it deals HP damage | never | - | never |
| `marker_modifier` | actor | actor | actor | actor | actor | actor |

`single_pc` redirects **heals only**. Buff tiers and stances test
`single_ally` exclusively, so on a `single_pc` move they land on the caster.
Use `single_ally` if a buff must reach the beneficiary.

`self` has no damage arm of its own, so `hp_damage` on a `self` move still
routes to the selected enemy. Use `set_self_damage` for genuine self-harm.

On `team_all` the caster takes the move's own HP and morale damage, classified
by its damage class. The HP share bypasses guard and the hit roll; the morale
share does not, so a caster in Dodge or Stealth consumes that stance and takes
no morale from its own blast.

A team-targeted move whose **entire** payload is utility is subject to a
separate admissibility gate (section 20).

---

## 8. Presence flags: the complete set

Every flag is written the same way:

```paradox
POD_combat_move_set_flag = { NAME = <flag> }
```

These 20 names are the whole contract. Anything else is an unused variable.

| Flag | Effect |
|---|---|
| `requires_hit_roll` | delivery: roll to hit (section 6) |
| `checks_guard` | delivery: Guard can block |
| `checks_stance` | delivery: Dodge and Stealth can evade |
| `checks_spirit_gate` | delivery: physical spirit gate applies |
| `requires_control_contact` | a payload-free move must land to apply its control effects |
| `bypass_dodge` | strip and ignore the target's Dodge |
| `bypass_stealth` | break and ignore the target's Stealth |
| `set_guard` | apply Guard. Blocks the next incoming move that checks guard, then is consumed |
| `dodge` | apply the Dodge stance |
| `stealth` | apply the Stealth stance, plus a hit bonus (30 by default) while it lasts |
| `remove_guard` | strip Guard from the hostile target, for later attackers too |
| `mind_control` | steal the target's next AI turn unless its mental defenses resist. Players are immune |
| `drain` | mark a damage-plus-heal move as a drain, for presentation and AI understanding |
| `dot_morale` | the move's damage-over-time ticks hit morale instead of HP |
| `retaliate_if_hit` | arm a counter that fires on an incoming HP-damage move that makes contact |
| `retaliate_if_missed` | arm a counter that fires when an incoming HP-damage move misses or is evaded |
| `retaliate_if_attacked` | arm one counter that answers either outcome |
| `summon_hostile` | seat the summoned creature on the side opposite the caster |
| `is_starter_move` | include the move in default player loadout seeding |
| `uses_weapon` | the move swings the actor's equipped weapon, so an artifact may retype its damage, add to it, make it undodgeable, or force it aggravated (the wielded-artifact bane list). Natural weapons and conjured blades are deliberately excluded. To grant the swing only while a condition holds, leave the flag off and use the `uses_weapon` bonus effect instead (section 16) |

`is_starter_move` is a combat-wide decision, not a synonym for "basic". The
seeder does **not** re-check the unlock rule, and starter status does not make
runtime access universal. Non-starters get an AI class-repertoire weight bonus.

`mind_control` should stay `single_enemy`: every AI weight for it is gated on
`single_enemy`, so an AoE mind-control move is effectively invisible to the AI.

`retaliate_agg`, `retaliate_morale`, `summons_combatant`, `summon_recipe` and
`marker_modifier` look like flags but have their own setters. See sections
11, 13 and 17.

