## 16. Bonus effects

With `MODE = bonus`, add exactly one effect.

```paradox
POD_combat_move_set_bonus = { EFFECT = energy_drain VALUE = 2 }
```

| `EFFECT` | `VALUE` means | Compatible with |
|---|---|---|
| `damage` | extra HP damage | a move with an HP damage path |
| `morale_damage` | extra morale damage | a hostile target |
| `change_type` | pass `0`; forces this hit aggravated | a move with HP damage |
| `hit` | added hit chance, recapped at 95 | a move that rolls to hit; **wiped on any team move** |
| `self_heal` | HP restored to the actor | anything |
| `heal_target` | HP restored to the selected target | single target only |
| `ap_refund` | AP returned to the actor | must stay strictly below `AP_COST` |
| `ap_drain` | AP removed from the selected target, next turn | `single-enemy` only, and at least 1 - both enforced; sums with a base `ap_drain_N` from `special` |
| `stance_guard` | pass `0` | the actor only |
| `stance_dodge` | pass `0` | the actor only |
| `stance_stealth` | pass `0` | the actor only |
| `energy_gain` | energy restored to the actor | anything |
| `energy_drain` | energy removed from the selected target | single target only |
| `dot` | damage per tick, fixed 2 rounds | `single_enemy` only; never alongside a base DoT (one slot, the second erases the first) |
| `morale_dot` | morale per tick, fixed 2 rounds | as `dot`; the tick erodes will instead of flesh and posts the morale affliction row |
| `self_morale_heal` | morale restored to the actor | the actor only - there is no target twin |
| `retaliate_boost` | damage added to the counter this move arms | requires a `retaliate_if_*` in `special`; boosts every family the move arms |
| `uses_weapon` | pass `0`; grants the weapon swing for this action | a move with an HP damage path, typed DoT or typed counter; never alongside the static `uses_weapon` flag |
| `change_class` | pass `0`; the element goes in `bonus_param` | a move with no authored `damage_type`, an HP/DoT/counter consumer, not Mental, not statically `uses_weapon` |

`change_type`, `change_class`, `uses_weapon` and the three `stance_*` effects
ignore `VALUE`; pass `0`. `change_class` is the only bonus with a second
column: `bonus_param` names one of the ten damage elements (there is no generic
"elemental" class), emitted as `POD_combat_move_set_bonus_param`.

`uses_weapon` is the odd one out: instead of a payload of its own it makes the
move swing the actor's equipped `primary_armament` for this action, so the
artifact's overrides empower it exactly as for a statically flagged move. Both
gates that read it (the section 2c profile seeder and the section 6 bane/soak
marker) go through `pod_combat_move_swings_weapon_trigger`.

`ap_refund` is a refund, not a discount: both affordability gates read the
gross `ap_cost`, so a move the actor cannot afford stays unclickable however
large its refund. Nothing in the engine clamps it below the cost.

A bonus should reward a distinct state, not reproduce the base payload every
use.

