## 20. Silent failures

None of these error, warn, or reach `error.log`.

| Trap | Consequence |
|---|---|
| A misspelled flag `NAME`, setter name, or value | An unused story variable. No effect, no error. |
| `set_damage_class` called before `set_hp_damage` | Overwritten back to `superficial`. |
| The setter block not immediately after its constructor | Setters apply to whichever move last claimed `scope:new_combat_move`. |
| A missing dispatcher leaf, or a misspelled `CONFIG` | The permissive fallback makes a restricted move available to everyone, while its decision still shows the requirement. |
| An unknown `PREDICATE` or `PARAM` | Fails closed. The condition is never true. |
| An unknown marker `KEY` | The section 12c switch has no fallback: nothing is stamped and nothing is raised. |
| A `heal_target` bonus with no loaded target (`self` or a team move) | Dereferences an unset workspace variable on the fight story at runtime. |
| A team move whose entire payload is `bypass_dodge` / `bypass_stealth` | Permanently greyed out: the pure-utility admissibility gate has no arm for it. |
| A `team_all` move carrying only buffs or stances | Same, and no broadcast arm exists for them either. |
| Buff tiers or stances on `single_pc` | They land on the caster, not the PC. |
| `hp_damage` on a `self` move | Still routes to the selected enemy. |
| A non-`always` rider on a morale-only move | The HP/contact axes were never established. |
| `mind_control` on any team targeting | Affects one target, and the AI's weights for it are gated on `single_enemy`. |
| `AP_COST = 0` with no `once_per` | Repeatable at zero cost; only the per-turn action cap bounds it. |
| Forgetting to increment `POD_current_combat_version` | Existing saves keep the old catalogue. |

The engine validates nothing about a move. The only automatic checks are CK3's
own identifier resolution and the script validator, and a new literal flag will
show up there as an unpaired set until it is registered in
`pod_combat_error_suppression_effects.txt`. Never add a suppression to hide a
real spelling or scope error.

